Time-reversibility paradox: In classical mechanics, the fundamental
laws of motion are time-symmetric, yet macroscopic physical processes
exhibit a preferred direction of time, creating a contradiction between
theory and observation.

"The camera is trapped inside a cubic space — a box where light falls
from above and shadows consume the edges. At its center, physical
simulation sequences play out — all in reverse. Each rigid-body scene
shown is actually a reversed replay of a simulation that was computed
in the background during the previous sequence. (The first simulation
runs while the intro is "loading".)"

Is reversed replay a betrayal of realtime, or a creative use of simu-
lation within technical constraints?


     *       watch it backwards. forward is a lie.      *
